IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wca-core`
IMPORT `wca-seat`

-- Cases for the injured worker's seat (wca-seat.l4), and the worker's regulative rules in wca-core.l4.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text (A1951-2.txt), never copied from the encoding's
-- output; the arithmetic is in the comment above each. No scenario life raised this Act: the workers and figures are
-- HYPOTHETICAL. The statutory floor, AWE and the indexed amounts are illustrative inputs (none is deposited); the lump
-- sums and death benefits use the Act's base figures, an index factor of 1.
--
-- Weekly question, 17 answers in this order: the day asked about; the initial incapacity date; the day of pension
-- age; the incapacity; average pre-incapacity weekly earnings; average pre-incapacity weekly hours; what is paid or
-- could be earned a week; hours a week working; weeks already counted; statutory floor now; pre-incapacity floor;
-- AWE; stopped living in Australia; likely permanent; absence helps recuperation; identity and incapacity proved;
-- imprisoned.
--
-- A breached or still-pending DEONTIC cannot be asserted on the stable l4, so regulative rules are asserted where the
-- trace ends FULFILLED, and #TRACEd with an "-- expect:" line where it does not.

`2 Mar 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 2 3 2026
`1 Oct 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2026
`15 Jun 2040` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 15 6 2040
`1 Jul 2027`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2027
`2 Mar 2028`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 2 3 2028
`3 Mar 2028`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 3 3 2028
`1 Jul 2030`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2030
`30 Jun 2030` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2030

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 1. Jim (the s 41 example, par (c)). HYPOTHETICAL figures: average pre-incapacity weekly earnings $1,500 over
-- 38 hours; statutory floor $900 a week before he was first incapacitated on 2 March 2026, $950 now; AWE $2,000.
-- Pension age far off (15 June 2040). Totally incapacitated.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Week 11 (10 weeks counted): s 39(4)(a), the average pre-incapacity weekly earnings: $1,500.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `1 Oct 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `15 Jun 2040` `totally incapacitated for work` 1500 38 0 0 10 950 900 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `weekly compensation, in dollars a week` 1500 "s 39(4)(a)"
-- After 26 weeks: 65% of 1500 = 975, more than the pre-incapacity floor 900, so s 41(1)(c): the more of 975 and the
-- statutory floor 950 = 975.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `1 Oct 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `15 Jun 2040` `totally incapacitated for work` 1500 38 0 0 26 950 900 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `weekly compensation, in dollars a week` 975 "s 41(1)(c)"
-- The same week with the statutory floor risen to 1000 at the time of payment: the more of 975 and 1000 = 1000.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `1 Oct 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `15 Jun 2040` `totally incapacitated for work` 1500 38 0 0 26 1000 900 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `weekly compensation, in dollars a week` 1000 "s 41(1)(c)"

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASES 2-4. The other paragraphs of s 41, and its gap. Pre-incapacity floor 900, statutory floor now 950.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Earnings $800, less than 900: s 41(1)(a), 100% of the earnings = 800 (no step-down).
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `1 Oct 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `15 Jun 2040` `totally incapacitated for work` 800 38 0 0 26 950 900 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `weekly compensation, in dollars a week` 800 "s 41(1)(a)"
-- Earnings $1,200: more than 900, but 65% = 780 is less than 900: s 41(1)(b), the statutory floor 950.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `1 Oct 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `15 Jun 2040` `totally incapacitated for work` 1200 38 0 0 26 950 900 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `weekly compensation, in dollars a week` 950 "s 41(1)(b)"
-- The same worker once the statutory floor has risen to 1300: s 41(1)(b) pays the statutory floor at the time of
-- payment, 1300, which is more than the 1200 he earned before the injury.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `1 Oct 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `15 Jun 2040` `totally incapacitated for work` 1200 38 0 0 26 1300 900 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `weekly compensation, in dollars a week` 1300 "s 41(1)(b)"
-- Earnings exactly the pre-incapacity floor (900 = 900): (a) needs "less", (b) needs "more", (c) needs 65% (585) more
-- than 900. No paragraph applies: not covered.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `1 Oct 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `15 Jun 2040` `totally incapacitated for work` 900 38 0 0 26 950 900 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `weekly compensation not covered` `s 41(1) says nothing where 100% or 65% of the earnings equals the pre-incapacity floor`
-- Earnings 1500 with a pre-incapacity floor of 975: 65% of 1500 = 975 exactly; (b) needs 65% less, (c) needs it more.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `1 Oct 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `15 Jun 2040` `totally incapacitated for work` 1500 38 0 0 26 1000 975 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `weekly compensation not covered` `s 41(1) says nothing where 100% or 65% of the earnings equals the pre-incapacity floor`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 5. Nicholas (the s 42 example 2). He earns the statutory floor: $950 a week over 38 hours (pre-incapacity floor
-- and statutory floor both 950). 6 weeks totally incapacitated, then partially incapacitated.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- (b)(i) of the example: the first 6 weeks, totally incapacitated: his earnings, 950.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `1 Oct 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `15 Jun 2040` `totally incapacitated for work` 950 38 0 0 0 950 950 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `weekly compensation, in dollars a week` 950 "s 39(4)(a)"
-- (b)(ii): partially incapacitated, light duties not provided, so no suitable employment reasonably available: 950 - 0.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `1 Oct 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `15 Jun 2040` `partially incapacitated for work` 950 38 0 0 6 950 950 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `weekly compensation, in dollars a week` 950 "s 39(4)(b)"
-- (b)(iii): working 20% of his hours (7.6 h) for 20% of his pay, 190: 950 - 190 = 760.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `1 Oct 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `15 Jun 2040` `partially incapacitated for work` 950 38 190 7.6 9 950 950 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `weekly compensation, in dollars a week` 760 "s 39(4)(b)"
-- Still within 26 weeks (19 counted), working 60% (22.8 h) for 570: 950 - 570 = 380.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `1 Oct 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `15 Jun 2040` `partially incapacitated for work` 950 38 570 22.8 19 950 950 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `weekly compensation, in dollars a week` 380 "s 39(4)(b)"
-- (b)(iv): after 26 weeks, 60% of hours: relevant percentage 85% (more than 50, not more than 75); 85% of 950 = 807.50,
-- less than the statutory floor 950, so s 42(1)(b): 950 - 570 = 380. ((a) does not apply: 950 is not less than 950.)
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `1 Oct 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `15 Jun 2040` `partially incapacitated for work` 950 38 570 22.8 26 950 950 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `weekly compensation, in dollars a week` 380 "s 42(1)(b)"

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 6. Bronwyn (the s 42 example 1). HYPOTHETICAL figures: $4,400 a week over 40 hours; she works 20 hours (50%) for
-- $2,200; AWE $2,000, so the statutory ceiling is 150% = 3,000; statutory floor 950.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- (a) of the example, within 26 weeks: the wages lost, 4400 - 2200 = 2200.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `1 Oct 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `15 Jun 2040` `partially incapacitated for work` 4400 40 2200 20 10 950 950 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `weekly compensation, in dollars a week` 2200 "s 39(4)(b)"
-- (b), after 26 weeks: 50% of hours gives 75%; 75% of 4400 = 3300, more than the ceiling 3000, so s 42(1)(c):
-- 3000 - 2200 = 800.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `1 Oct 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `15 Jun 2040` `partially incapacitated for work` 4400 40 2200 20 26 950 950 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `weekly compensation, in dollars a week` 800 "s 42(1)(c)"

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASES 7-8. s 42(1)(d) and (a), and the nil floor.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- $2,000 over 40 hours, now 32 hours (80%: 95%) for $1,600. 95% of 2000 = 1900: not below 950, not above 3000, so (d):
-- 1900 - 1600 = 300.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `1 Oct 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `15 Jun 2040` `partially incapacitated for work` 2000 40 1600 32 30 950 950 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `weekly compensation, in dollars a week` 300 "s 42(1)(d)"
-- $800 over 40 hours (below the floor 950), now 10 hours (25%: 65%) for $200: (a) 100% of 800, less 200 = 600.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `1 Oct 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `15 Jun 2040` `partially incapacitated for work` 800 40 200 10 30 950 950 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `weekly compensation, in dollars a week` 600 "s 42(1)(a)"
-- Within 26 weeks, earning more in suitable work (1200) than before (1000): the difference is read as never below nil.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `1 Oct 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `15 Jun 2040` `partially incapacitated for work` 1000 40 1200 40 3 950 950 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `weekly compensation, in dollars a week` 0 "s 39(4)(b)"

-- s 42(2) relevant percentages, of 40 pre-incapacity hours: not working 65%; 10 h (25%) 65%; 11 h (27.5%) 75%;
-- 20 h (50%) 75%; 30 h (75%) 85%; 34 h (85%) 95%; 35 h (87.5%) 100%.
#ASSERT `What is my relevant percentage after 26 weeks` 0 40 EQUALS 0.65
#ASSERT `What is my relevant percentage after 26 weeks` 10 40 EQUALS 0.65
#ASSERT `What is my relevant percentage after 26 weeks` 11 40 EQUALS 0.75
#ASSERT `What is my relevant percentage after 26 weeks` 20 40 EQUALS 0.75
#ASSERT `What is my relevant percentage after 26 weeks` 30 40 EQUALS 0.85
#ASSERT `What is my relevant percentage after 26 weeks` 34 40 EQUALS 0.95
#ASSERT `What is my relevant percentage after 26 weeks` 35 40 EQUALS 1

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 9. The age limits (s 39(3), s 40(4)). First incapacitated 2 March 2026.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Pension age 15 June 2040: more than 2 years away, so no weekly compensation from that day.
#ASSERT `When does my weekly compensation stop because of my age` `2 Mar 2026` `15 Jun 2040` EQUALS `no weekly compensation from the day the worker reaches pension age` `15 Jun 2040`
-- Pension age 1 July 2027: 2 years or less away, so nothing after 2 March 2028.
#ASSERT `When does my weekly compensation stop because of my age` `2 Mar 2026` `1 Jul 2027` EQUALS `no weekly compensation for any day after the second anniversary of the initial incapacity date` `2 Mar 2028`
-- Pension age exactly 2 years away (2 March 2028): "by 2 years or less", the same day.
#ASSERT `When does my weekly compensation stop because of my age` `2 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2028` EQUALS `no weekly compensation for any day after the second anniversary of the initial incapacity date` `2 Mar 2028`
-- Already over pension age (reached 1 January 2020): s 39(3)(d), 2 years after.
#ASSERT `When does my weekly compensation stop because of my age` `2 Mar 2026` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2020) EQUALS `no weekly compensation for any day after the second anniversary of the initial incapacity date` `2 Mar 2028`
-- First incapacitated 29 February 2028: read as 28 February 2030.
#ASSERT `When does my weekly compensation stop because of my age` (DATE_FROM_DMY 29 2 2028) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2029) EQUALS `no weekly compensation for any day after the second anniversary of the initial incapacity date` (DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2030)
-- Jim's facts after 26 weeks (975), with pension age 1 July 2027: still paid on 2 March 2028, not on 3 March 2028.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `2 Mar 2028` `2 Mar 2026` `1 Jul 2027` `totally incapacitated for work` 1500 38 0 0 26 950 900 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `weekly compensation, in dollars a week` 975 "s 41(1)(c)"
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `3 Mar 2028` `2 Mar 2026` `1 Jul 2027` `totally incapacitated for work` 1500 38 0 0 26 950 900 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no weekly compensation` `the age limit in s 39(3) and s 40(4) has passed`
-- With pension age 1 July 2030: paid on 30 June 2030, not from 1 July 2030.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `30 Jun 2030` `2 Mar 2026` `1 Jul 2030` `totally incapacitated for work` 1500 38 0 0 26 950 900 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `weekly compensation, in dollars a week` 975 "s 41(1)(c)"
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `1 Jul 2030` `2 Mar 2026` `1 Jul 2030` `totally incapacitated for work` 1500 38 0 0 26 950 900 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no weekly compensation` `the age limit in s 39(3) and s 40(4) has passed`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASES 10-11. Living outside Australia (ss 44-45), prison (s 83), no incapacity, death (s 37). Jim's facts, 975.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Moved overseas; incapacity not likely permanent; absence does not help recovery: no weekly compensation (s 44(1)).
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `1 Oct 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `15 Jun 2040` `totally incapacitated for work` 1500 38 0 0 26 950 900 2000 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no weekly compensation` `the worker has stopped living in Australia (s 44(1))`
-- Likely permanent, identity and incapacity proved: paid quarterly, at the weekly amount (s 45(2)).
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `1 Oct 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `15 Jun 2040` `totally incapacitated for work` 1500 38 0 0 26 950 900 2000 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `paid quarterly while living outside Australia (s 45), in dollars a week` 975 "s 41(1)(c)"
-- Absence helps recovery, but identity and incapacity not proved: nothing (s 45(3)).
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `1 Oct 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `15 Jun 2040` `totally incapacitated for work` 1500 38 0 0 26 950 900 2000 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no weekly compensation` `the worker lives outside Australia and has not proved identity and continuing incapacity (s 45(3))`
-- In prison after a conviction: nothing (s 83).
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `1 Oct 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `15 Jun 2040` `totally incapacitated for work` 1500 38 0 0 26 950 900 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no weekly compensation` `the worker is imprisoned after a conviction (s 83)`
-- Back to full capacity: nothing for the week (s 43(1)(a)).
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation am I paid this week` `1 Oct 2026` `2 Mar 2026` `15 Jun 2040` `not incapacitated for work` 1500 38 1500 38 26 950 950 2000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no weekly compensation` `the worker is not incapacitated for work because of the injury`

-- s 37, on the core: Jim's week, but the worker has died.
`Jim's week after his death` MEANS
    `Weekly facts` WITH
        `the day asked about`                                         IS `1 Oct 2026`
        `the initial incapacity date`                                 IS `2 Mar 2026`
        `the day the worker reaches pension age`                      IS `15 Jun 2040`
        `the worker is`                                               IS `totally incapacitated for work`
        `average pre-incapacity weekly earnings`                      IS 1500
        `average pre-incapacity weekly hours`                         IS 38
        `the weekly amount the worker is paid for working or could earn in reasonably available suitable employment` IS 0
        `the hours a week the worker is working`                      IS 0
        `weeks of weekly compensation already counted under s 39`     IS 26
        `the statutory floor at the time of payment`                  IS 950
        `the pre-incapacity floor`                                    IS 900
        `AWE at the time of payment`                                  IS 2000
        `the worker is dead`                                          IS TRUE
        `the worker has stopped living in Australia`                  IS FALSE
        `the incapacity is likely to be permanent`                    IS FALSE
        `the absence from Australia is likely to help the worker recuperate` IS FALSE
        `the worker proves identity and continuing incapacity`        IS FALSE
        `the worker is imprisoned after a conviction`                 IS FALSE
#ASSERT `the weekly compensation for` `Jim's week after his death` EQUALS `no weekly compensation` `the worker is dead (s 37), apart from weekly compensation that accrued before death`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 12. Claiming within 7 days (s 38(2), (3)). Injured Thursday 1 October 2026.
-- =====================================================================================================================

`8 Oct 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 8 10 2026
`9 Oct 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 9 10 2026
`14 Oct 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 14 10 2026
`15 Oct 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 15 10 2026
`20 Oct 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 20 10 2026
`27 Oct 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 27 10 2026
`28 Oct 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 28 10 2026

-- The 7 days after 1 October end on 8 October.
#ASSERT `By what day must I claim to keep my weekly payments going` `1 Oct 2026` FALSE `1 Oct 2026` EQUALS `8 Oct 2026`
-- Unable to claim because of the injury until 20 October: 7 days after that, 27 October.
#ASSERT `By what day must I claim to keep my weekly payments going` `1 Oct 2026` TRUE `20 Oct 2026` EQUALS `27 Oct 2026`
-- Claim on 8 October: in time, nothing lost.
#ASSERT `Do I lose weekly compensation because I claimed late` `1 Oct 2026` `8 Oct 2026` FALSE `1 Oct 2026` EQUALS `no weekly compensation is lost under s 38(2)`
-- Claim on 9 October: late, but the lost period would run from 9 October (8 days after) to 8 October (the day before
-- the claim): empty, so nothing is lost.
#ASSERT `Do I lose weekly compensation because I claimed late` `1 Oct 2026` `9 Oct 2026` FALSE `1 Oct 2026` EQUALS `no weekly compensation is lost under s 38(2)`
-- Claim on 15 October: nothing from 9 October to 14 October.
#ASSERT `Do I lose weekly compensation because I claimed late` `1 Oct 2026` `15 Oct 2026` FALSE `1 Oct 2026` EQUALS `no weekly compensation for the days` `9 Oct 2026` `14 Oct 2026`
-- Prevented until 20 October, claimed 27 October: s 38(3) applies, nothing lost.
#ASSERT `Do I lose weekly compensation because I claimed late` `1 Oct 2026` `27 Oct 2026` TRUE `20 Oct 2026` EQUALS `no weekly compensation is lost under s 38(2)`
-- Prevented until 20 October, but claimed 28 October: s 38(3)(b) fails, so s 38(2) applies in full, from 9 October to
-- 27 October.
#ASSERT `Do I lose weekly compensation because I claimed late` `1 Oct 2026` `28 Oct 2026` TRUE `20 Oct 2026` EQUALS `no weekly compensation for the days` `9 Oct 2026` `27 Oct 2026`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 13. Lump sums for permanent injuries. Single loss amount $100,000, maximum loss amount $150,000 (index 1).
-- Question 1 answers: item; % lost; deductible %; deductible hard to work out; only limb; left-dominant; penis; testicles.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Loss of the right arm at or above the elbow (item 12): 80%.
#ASSERT `What percentage of the single loss amount is my loss worth` 12 100 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `my loss is worth this percentage of the single loss amount` 80
-- The s 61 example: 30% loss of use of the right arm, deductible proportion hard to work out, so 10% of the loss:
-- 80 x 30% = 24, less 10% = 21.6.
#ASSERT `What percentage of the single loss amount is my loss worth` 12 30 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `my loss is worth this percentage of the single loss amount` 21.6
-- s 54: a left-handed worker loses the left arm at or above the elbow (item 14, 75%): compensated as item 12, 80%.
#ASSERT `What percentage of the single loss amount is my loss worth` 14 100 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS `my loss is worth this percentage of the single loss amount` 80
-- ... and the right arm (item 12) as item 14, 75%.
#ASSERT `What percentage of the single loss amount is my loss worth` 12 100 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS `my loss is worth this percentage of the single loss amount` 75
-- s 56: an only leg at or above the knee, as both legs: 75 + 75 = 150.
#ASSERT `What percentage of the single loss amount is my loss worth` 33 100 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `my loss is worth this percentage of the single loss amount` 150
-- s 56: an only arm at or above the elbow, as both arms: 80 + 75 = 155.
#ASSERT `What percentage of the single loss amount is my loss worth` 12 100 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `my loss is worth this percentage of the single loss amount` 155
-- s 56 says nothing of eyes: the "only limb" answer is ignored for the sight of 1 eye (item 9), 40.
#ASSERT `What percentage of the single loss amount is my loss worth` 9 100 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `my loss is worth this percentage of the single loss amount` 40
-- s 57: loss of 1 testicle, 10; penis and 1 testicle, 47 + 10 = 57 capped at 47; an only testicle (counts as 2), 47.
#ASSERT `What percentage of the single loss amount is my loss worth` 41 100 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 EQUALS `my loss is worth this percentage of the single loss amount` 10
#ASSERT `What percentage of the single loss amount is my loss worth` 41 100 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 1 EQUALS `my loss is worth this percentage of the single loss amount` 47
#ASSERT `What percentage of the single loss amount is my loss worth` 41 100 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 2 EQUALS `my loss is worth this percentage of the single loss amount` 47
-- Item 41 for another sexual organ (neither penis nor testicle): item 41's 47.
#ASSERT `What percentage of the single loss amount is my loss worth` 41 100 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `my loss is worth this percentage of the single loss amount` 47
-- Back (item 46, 60%), 40% impairment, a known 25% of it from an earlier injury: 60 x 40% = 24, less 25% = 18.
#ASSERT `What percentage of the single loss amount is my loss worth` 46 40 25 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `my loss is worth this percentage of the single loss amount` 18
-- Item 99 is not in schedule 1.
#ASSERT `What percentage of the single loss amount is my loss worth` 99 100 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `my lump sum is not covered` `the item is not one of the 54 items of Schedule 1`

-- In dollars: item 12, 80% of 100,000 = 80,000.
#ASSERT `How much is my lump sum for a permanent loss` 12 100 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 100000 150000 EQUALS `my lump sum, in dollars, is` 80000
-- The s 61 example: 21.6% of 100,000 = 21,600.
#ASSERT `How much is my lump sum for a permanent loss` 12 30 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 100000 150000 EQUALS `my lump sum, in dollars, is` 21600
-- An only arm at or above the elbow: 155% of 100,000 = 155,000, capped at the maximum loss amount 150,000.
#ASSERT `How much is my lump sum for a permanent loss` 12 100 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 100000 150000 EQUALS `my lump sum, in dollars, is` 150000
-- HYPOTHETICAL indexed amounts (index factor 1.3125): single loss 131,250, maximum 196,875; sight of 1 eye, 40% =
-- 52,500.
#ASSERT `How much is my lump sum for a permanent loss` 9 100 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 131250 196875 EQUALS `my lump sum, in dollars, is` 52500
#ASSERT `How much is my lump sum for a permanent loss` 99 100 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 100000 150000 EQUALS `my lump sum is not covered` `the item is not one of the 54 items of Schedule 1`

-- Two losses (s 53). Sight of 1 eye (40) and 50% of the back (60 x 50% = 30): 70% = 70,000.
#ASSERT `How much is my lump sum for two permanent losses` 9 100 0 FALSE FALSE 46 50 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 100000 150000 EQUALS `my lump sum, in dollars, is` 70000
-- Sight of 1 eye (40) and the eyeball, "in addition" (22): 62% = 62,000.
#ASSERT `How much is my lump sum for two permanent losses` 9 100 0 FALSE FALSE 11 100 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 100000 150000 EQUALS `my lump sum, in dollars, is` 62000
-- A leg at or above the knee (75) and the right arm at or above the elbow (80): 155% = 155,000, capped at 150,000.
#ASSERT `How much is my lump sum for two permanent losses` 33 100 0 FALSE FALSE 12 100 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 100000 150000 EQUALS `my lump sum, in dollars, is` 150000
-- One item not in schedule 1: not covered.
#ASSERT `How much is my lump sum for two permanent losses` 9 100 0 FALSE FALSE 77 100 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 100000 150000 EQUALS `my lump sum is not covered` `the item is not one of the 54 items of Schedule 1`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 14. When the lump sum may be claimed (s 121). Injured 15 January 2026.
-- =====================================================================================================================

`15 Jan 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 15 1 2026
`15 Jan 2028` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 15 1 2028

-- Not stabilised, no court order: not before 15 January 2028.
#ASSERT `When can I claim my lump sum` `15 Jan 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a lump sum claim may not be made before` `15 Jan 2028`
-- Back at full hours for at least 3 months: stabilised, claim now.
#ASSERT `When can I claim my lump sum` `15 Jan 2026` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a lump sum claim may be made now (s 121(2))`
-- Back at full hours, but under 3 months: not yet stabilised under s 121(4).
#ASSERT `When can I claim my lump sum` `15 Jan 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a lump sum claim may not be made before` `15 Jan 2028`
-- Stabilised without going back (s 121(5)): now. The court allows an early claim: now.
#ASSERT `When can I claim my lump sum` `15 Jan 2026` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `a lump sum claim may be made now (s 121(2))`
#ASSERT `When can I claim my lump sum` `15 Jan 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a lump sum claim may be made now (s 121(2))`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 15. Indexing (s 20, s 77(7)).
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- The s 20 example: $100, CPI 100 -> 120 -> 108 -> 129.60. The highest ratio reached is 1.296: $129.60.
#ASSERT `the cpi indexed amount` 100 100 129.6 EQUALS 129.6
-- At the 108 stage of the example the highest CPI so far is 120: the amount stays $120 (not $108).
#ASSERT `the cpi indexed amount` 100 100 120 EQUALS 120
-- A CPI that has only fallen since commencement leaves the figure where it was.
#ASSERT `the cpi indexed amount` 100 100 95 EQUALS 100
-- HYPOTHETICAL: CPI 80 at commencement, highest since 100: the single loss amount is 100,000 x 1.25 = 125,000.
#ASSERT `What is this indexed amount worth now` `the single loss amount (s 49)` 80 100 EQUALS 125000
-- Funeral maximum, CPI up 4%: 11,828.87 x 1.04 = 12,302.0248.
#ASSERT `What is this indexed amount worth now` `the funeral expenses maximum (s 77(2)(c), (6))` 100 104 EQUALS 12302.0248
-- Death lump sum, WPI up 10%: 539,002.37 x 1.1 = 592,902.607.
#ASSERT `What is this indexed amount worth now` `the death lump sum (s 77(2)(a))` 100 110 EQUALS 592902.607
-- Child weekly payment, WPI up 20%: 148.23 x 1.2 = 177.876.
#ASSERT `What is this indexed amount worth now` `the weekly payment for each dependent child (s 77(2)(b))` 100 120 EQUALS 177.876
-- A WPI fall of 2%: s 20(2) does not reach wpi indexing, so read literally: 539,002.37 x 0.98 = 528,222.3226.
#ASSERT `What is this indexed amount worth now` `the death lump sum (s 77(2)(a))` 100 98 EQUALS 528222.3226

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 16. Death (s 77). Base figures: lump sum 539,002.37; 148.23 a week for each child; funeral maximum 11,828.87.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- A domestic partner who depended on the worker's earnings: a dependant.
#ASSERT `Am I a dependant of the worker who died` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- A friend who depended on the worker but was not family, and not in a parent relationship: not a dependant.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Am I a dependant of the worker who died` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- A grandchild who depended only through family tax benefit (left out by s 77(3)): not dependent, so not a dependant.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Am I a dependant of the worker who died` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
-- A foster child the worker raised, who would have depended on the worker but for the incapacity: a dependant.
#ASSERT `Am I a dependant of the worker who died` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE

-- The worker's child: 15 (yes); 19 and a full-time student (yes); 24 and a full-time student (yes); 19 not studying
-- (no); 16 not studying (no); 25 and a student (no); 17 in a domestic partnership (no); a grandchild of 10 (no: not the
-- worker's child).
#ASSERT `Is this dependant paid weekly compensation as the worker's child` TRUE FALSE 15 FALSE
#ASSERT `Is this dependant paid weekly compensation as the worker's child` TRUE FALSE 19 TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this dependant paid weekly compensation as the worker's child` TRUE FALSE 24 TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is this dependant paid weekly compensation as the worker's child` TRUE FALSE 19 FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is this dependant paid weekly compensation as the worker's child` TRUE FALSE 16 FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is this dependant paid weekly compensation as the worker's child` TRUE FALSE 25 TRUE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is this dependant paid weekly compensation as the worker's child` TRUE TRUE 17 TRUE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is this dependant paid weekly compensation as the worker's child` FALSE FALSE 10 FALSE))

-- Three dependants, two of them children; funeral $15,000. The lump sum 539,002.37 goes to the dependants (through the
-- court); 148.23 a week for each child, 296.46 for both; funeral capped at 11,828.87.
#ASSERT (`What do the dependants get when the worker dies` TRUE 3 2 15000 539002.37 148.23 11828.87)'s `paid to` EQUALS `the dependants: the lump sum is paid into the Magistrates Court and divided as it considers appropriate (ss 77(4), 78)`
#ASSERT (`What do the dependants get when the worker dies` TRUE 3 2 15000 539002.37 148.23 11828.87)'s `the lump sum to be divided between the dependants` EQUALS 539002.37
#ASSERT (`What do the dependants get when the worker dies` TRUE 3 2 15000 539002.37 148.23 11828.87)'s `weekly compensation for each dependent child` EQUALS 148.23
#ASSERT (`What do the dependants get when the worker dies` TRUE 3 2 15000 539002.37 148.23 11828.87)'s `weekly compensation for all the dependent children` EQUALS 296.46
#ASSERT (`What do the dependants get when the worker dies` TRUE 3 2 15000 539002.37 148.23 11828.87)'s `funeral expenses payable` EQUALS 11828.87
-- One dependant, no children, funeral $8,000: the lump sum, no weekly payment, funeral 8,000 (under the cap).
#ASSERT (`What do the dependants get when the worker dies` TRUE 1 0 8000 539002.37 148.23 11828.87)'s `weekly compensation for all the dependent children` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`What do the dependants get when the worker dies` TRUE 1 0 8000 539002.37 148.23 11828.87)'s `funeral expenses payable` EQUALS 8000
-- No dependants, funeral $9,000: the personal representative gets the funeral expenses only (s 77(6)).
#ASSERT (`What do the dependants get when the worker dies` TRUE 0 0 9000 539002.37 148.23 11828.87)'s `paid to` EQUALS `the personal representative: funeral expenses only (s 77(6))`
#ASSERT (`What do the dependants get when the worker dies` TRUE 0 0 9000 539002.37 148.23 11828.87)'s `the lump sum to be divided between the dependants` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`What do the dependants get when the worker dies` TRUE 0 0 9000 539002.37 148.23 11828.87)'s `funeral expenses payable` EQUALS 9000
-- No compensation payable for the death (an intentionally self-inflicted injury, s 82(2)): nothing.
#ASSERT (`What do the dependants get when the worker dies` FALSE 2 1 9000 539002.37 148.23 11828.87)'s `paid to` EQUALS `no one: compensation is not payable under the Act for the death (s 77(1))`
#ASSERT (`What do the dependants get when the worker dies` FALSE 2 1 9000 539002.37 148.23 11828.87)'s `funeral expenses payable` EQUALS 0

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASES 17-18. When the claim is made (s 119, s 122) and the 3 years (s 120).
-- =====================================================================================================================

`5 Nov 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 5 11 2026
`20 Nov 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 20 11 2026

-- Given to the employer on 5 November with a complying certificate: made 5 November.
#ASSERT `On what day is my claim made` `5 Nov 2026` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `20 Nov 2026` EQUALS `5 Nov 2026`
-- Deficient certificate, flagged in writing within 72 hours; complying certificate on 20 November: made 20 November.
#ASSERT `On what day is my claim made` `5 Nov 2026` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `20 Nov 2026` EQUALS `20 Nov 2026`
-- Deficient, but not flagged within 72 hours: taken to comply, made 5 November (s 119(3)).
#ASSERT `On what day is my claim made` `5 Nov 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `20 Nov 2026` EQUALS `5 Nov 2026`
-- Deficient and flagged, but the insurer waived the requirement: made 5 November (s 119(4)).
#ASSERT `On what day is my claim made` `5 Nov 2026` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `20 Nov 2026` EQUALS `5 Nov 2026`
-- A lump sum claim needs no s 116(2) certificate: made 5 November.
#ASSERT `On what day is my claim made` `5 Nov 2026` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `20 Nov 2026` EQUALS `5 Nov 2026`

-- Injured 1 October 2026 and aware of it: claim by 1 October 2029.
#ASSERT `By what day must my claim be made` `1 Oct 2026` TRUE `1 Oct 2026` FALSE `1 Oct 2026` EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2029
-- A disease noticed on 1 March 2027: claim by 1 March 2030.
#ASSERT `By what day must my claim be made` `1 Oct 2026` FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2027) FALSE `1 Oct 2026` EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2030
-- A claim for the worker's death, the claimant aware of it on 10 January 2027: by 10 January 2030.
#ASSERT `By what day must my claim be made` `1 Oct 2026` TRUE `1 Oct 2026` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2027) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2030
-- Injured on 29 February 2028: read as 28 February 2031.
#ASSERT `By what day must my claim be made` (DATE_FROM_DMY 29 2 2028) TRUE `1 Oct 2026` FALSE `1 Oct 2026` EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2031
-- Notice in time, claim on the last day (1 October 2029): the proceeding may continue.
#ASSERT `May my proceeding for compensation continue` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2029) `1 Oct 2026` TRUE `1 Oct 2026` FALSE `1 Oct 2026` EQUALS `the proceeding may continue (s 120(1))`
-- Claim a day late: only with the court's leave (s 120A) or under s 124.
#ASSERT `May my proceeding for compensation continue` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 10 2029) `1 Oct 2026` TRUE `1 Oct 2026` FALSE `1 Oct 2026` EQUALS `the proceeding may continue only if the Magistrates Court allows it (s 120A) or s 124 applies`
-- Claim in time, but notice not given as soon as practicable: likewise.
#ASSERT `May my proceeding for compensation continue` FALSE `5 Nov 2026` `1 Oct 2026` TRUE `1 Oct 2026` FALSE `1 Oct 2026` EQUALS `the proceeding may continue only if the Magistrates Court allows it (s 120A) or s 124 applies`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASES 19-20. Acceptance by silence (s 128) and stopping after a rejection (ss 129-132). Claim given to and received
-- by the insurer on 2 November 2026.
-- =====================================================================================================================

`2 Nov 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 2 11 2026
`30 Nov 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 11 2026
`1 Dec 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2026

-- No decision: taken to be accepted at the end of 30 November 2026 (2 November + 28 days).
#ASSERT `Is my claim taken to be accepted` FALSE `2 Nov 2026` FALSE `2 Nov 2026` EQUALS `the claim is taken to be accepted at the end of` `30 Nov 2026`
-- Decided to reject on 30 November, the 28th day: in time, not accepted.
#ASSERT `Is my claim taken to be accepted` FALSE `2 Nov 2026` TRUE `30 Nov 2026` EQUALS `the claim is not taken to be accepted: the insurer decided to reject it within 28 days`
-- Decided on 1 December, too late: accepted at the end of 30 November.
#ASSERT `Is my claim taken to be accepted` FALSE `2 Nov 2026` TRUE `1 Dec 2026` EQUALS `the claim is taken to be accepted at the end of` `30 Nov 2026`
-- Decided to reject on 29 November (day 27): not taken to be accepted, although the rejection takes effect only when
-- the notice is received (s 129(2)) ...
#ASSERT `Is my claim taken to be accepted` FALSE `2 Nov 2026` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 29 11 2026) EQUALS `the claim is not taken to be accepted: the insurer decided to reject it within 28 days`
-- ... and if the notice reaches the worker and employer on 2 December (day 30), it is a rejection "28 days or later":
-- 8 weeks, 2 December + 29 = 31 December, + 27 = 27 January 2027.
#ASSERT `From what day may my weekly compensation stop after a rejection` `2 Nov 2026` (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 12 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `2 Nov 2026` EQUALS `weekly compensation may stop from` (DATE_FROM_DMY 27 1 2027) "s 131(a)"
-- An imminently fatal asbestos-related disease: not covered.
#ASSERT `Is my claim taken to be accepted` TRUE `2 Nov 2026` FALSE `2 Nov 2026` EQUALS `acceptance not covered` `a claim for an imminently fatal asbestos-related disease (ss 116(2)(a), 121(2)(a), 122(1)(a), 128A) is outside this encoding`

-- Stop question answers: claim given; rejection received; reasons given; only ground no time; court leave; order
-- states a day; the day stated; the day the worker got notice.
-- Rejected (notice received) 20 November, day 18, with reasons: s 130, 2 weeks: from 4 December 2026.
#ASSERT `From what day may my weekly compensation stop after a rejection` `2 Nov 2026` `20 Nov 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `2 Nov 2026` EQUALS `weekly compensation may stop from` (DATE_FROM_DMY 4 12 2026) "s 130(1)(a)"
-- Rejected 30 November, day 28: still "within 28 days" on the encoded reading: 2 weeks, from 14 December 2026.
#ASSERT `From what day may my weekly compensation stop after a rejection` `2 Nov 2026` `30 Nov 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `2 Nov 2026` EQUALS `weekly compensation may stop from` (DATE_FROM_DMY 14 12 2026) "s 130(1)(a)"
-- Rejected 1 December, day 29: s 131, 8 weeks (56 days): 1 December + 30 = 31 December, + 26 = 26 January 2027.
#ASSERT `From what day may my weekly compensation stop after a rejection` `2 Nov 2026` `1 Dec 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `2 Nov 2026` EQUALS `weekly compensation may stop from` (DATE_FROM_DMY 26 1 2027) "s 131(a)"
-- Rejected 2 November 2027, exactly 1 year: s 131 on the encoded reading; 2 November + 28 = 30 November, + 28 =
-- 28 December 2027.
#ASSERT `From what day may my weekly compensation stop after a rejection` `2 Nov 2026` (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 11 2027) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `2 Nov 2026` EQUALS `weekly compensation may stop from` (DATE_FROM_DMY 28 12 2027) "s 131(a)"
-- Rejected 3 November 2027, without the court's leave: no effect; payments continue (s 132(1), s 134).
#ASSERT `From what day may my weekly compensation stop after a rejection` `2 Nov 2026` (DATE_FROM_DMY 3 11 2027) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `2 Nov 2026` EQUALS `the rejection does not let weekly compensation stop: the insurer stays liable until it rejects or settles (s 134(1))` `from 1 year the insurer may reject only with the Magistrates Court's leave (s 132(1))`
-- With leave, the order stating 1 December 2027: from that day.
#ASSERT `From what day may my weekly compensation stop after a rejection` `2 Nov 2026` (DATE_FROM_DMY 3 11 2027) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2027) `2 Nov 2026` EQUALS `weekly compensation may stop from` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2027) "s 132(2)(b)(i)"
-- With leave, no day stated, the worker got notice on 10 November 2027: 8 weeks later, 10 November + 20 = 30 November,
-- + 31 = 31 December, + 5 = 5 January 2028.
#ASSERT `From what day may my weekly compensation stop after a rejection` `2 Nov 2026` (DATE_FROM_DMY 3 11 2027) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `2 Nov 2026` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 11 2027) EQUALS `weekly compensation may stop from` (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 1 2028) "s 132(2)(b)(ii)"
-- Rejected within 28 days only because the insurer had no time to assess: not allowed (s 130(2)).
#ASSERT `From what day may my weekly compensation stop after a rejection` `2 Nov 2026` `20 Nov 2026` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `2 Nov 2026` EQUALS `the rejection does not let weekly compensation stop: the insurer stays liable until it rejects or settles (s 134(1))` `the only ground is that the insurer has not had time to assess the claim (s 130(2))`
-- A notice that says only "medical reasons": no reason given, no rejection (s 129(4), (6)).
#ASSERT `From what day may my weekly compensation stop after a rejection` `2 Nov 2026` `20 Nov 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `2 Nov 2026` EQUALS `the rejection does not let weekly compensation stop: the insurer stays liable until it rejects or settles (s 134(1))` `the notice does not give the reason for rejecting the claim (s 129(4)-(6))`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- Regulative rules (wca-core.l4). Clock in days; day 0 is the day the rule starts.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- s 93(1), s 38(1): the worker tells the employer on day 2 and the employer begins weekly payments that day: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 93(1), s 38(1) -- the worker tells the employer, and the employer must then begin weekly payments` TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker` `tell the employer about the injury` 2), (EVENT `the employer` `begin paying weekly compensation` 2)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- A worker who is not and may not be entitled: telling the employer ends the matter.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 93(1), s 38(1) -- the worker tells the employer, and the employer must then begin weekly payments` FALSE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker` `tell the employer about the injury` 2)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the employer, "s 38(1)(a), (4): the employer must begin weekly compensation when ..." (began a day late)
#TRACE `s 93(1), s 38(1) -- the worker tells the employer, and the employer must then begin weekly payments` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the worker` DOES `tell the employer about the injury` AT 2
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `begin paying weekly compensation` AT 3
-- expect: the worker's obligation still pending ("as soon as possible" sets no day, so time alone never breaches it)
#TRACE `s 93(1), s 38(1) -- the worker tells the employer, and the employer must then begin weekly payments` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- s 38(2): 7 days. A claim on day 5, or on day 7: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 38(2), (3) -- a claim within 7 days keeps weekly payments going, or they may stop` 7) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker` `make a claim for compensation` 5)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 38(2), (3) -- a claim within 7 days keeps weekly payments going, or they may stop` 7) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker` `make a claim for compensation` 7)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- No claim by day 7; on day 9 the employer stops paying, as it may: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 38(2), (3) -- a claim within 7 days keeps weekly payments going, or they may stop` 7) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 8), (EVENT `the employer` `stop paying weekly compensation` 9)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the employer's permission to stop paying weekly compensation, open (no claim by day 7)
#TRACE `s 38(2), (3) -- a claim within 7 days keeps weekly payments going, or they may stop` 7 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 8)
-- s 38(3): injured 1 October, first able to claim 20 October: the days run to 27 October, 26 days from the injury.
#ASSERT `days from` `1 Oct 2026` `to` (`By what day must I claim to keep my weekly payments going` `1 Oct 2026` TRUE `20 Oct 2026`) EQUALS 26
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 38(2), (3) -- a claim within 7 days keeps weekly payments going, or they may stop` 26) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker` `make a claim for compensation` 26)) EQUALS FULFILLED

-- s 120: from 1 October 2026 to 1 October 2029 is 365 + 366 (29 February 2028) + 365 = 1096 days.
#ASSERT `days from` `1 Oct 2026` `to` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2029) EQUALS 1096
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 120 -- the claim is made within 3 years, or only the Magistrates Court can let the proceeding continue` 1096) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker` `make a claim for compensation` 1096)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Out of time; the worker applies to the Magistrates Court under s 120A: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 120 -- the claim is made within 3 years, or only the Magistrates Court can let the proceeding continue` 1096) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 1097), (EVENT `the worker` `apply to the Magistrates Court to allow the late claim` 1100)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the worker's permission to apply to the Magistrates Court, open (no claim within the 3 years)
#TRACE `s 120 -- the claim is made within 3 years, or only the Magistrates Court can let the proceeding continue` 1096 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 1097)

-- s 121: from 15 January 2026 to 15 January 2028 is 365 + 365 = 730 days. A claim on day 730: fulfilled.
#ASSERT `days from` `15 Jan 2026` `to` `15 Jan 2028` EQUALS 730
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 121 -- no permanent injury claim earlier than 2 years after the injury, unless it has stabilised or the court allows` 730 FALSE FALSE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker` `make a claim for a permanent injury lump sum` 730)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Stabilised, or allowed by the court: a claim on day 100 is fine.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 121 -- no permanent injury claim earlier than 2 years after the injury, unless it has stabilised or the court allows` 730 TRUE FALSE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker` `make a claim for a permanent injury lump sum` 100)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 121 -- no permanent injury claim earlier than 2 years after the injury, unless it has stabilised or the court allows` 730 FALSE TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker` `make a claim for a permanent injury lump sum` 100)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the worker, "s 121(1): a claim under part 4.4 may not be made earlier than 2 years ..." (day 700)
#TRACE `s 121 -- no permanent injury claim earlier than 2 years after the injury, unless it has stabilised or the court allows` 730 FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the worker` DOES `make a claim for a permanent injury lump sum` AT 700
